    "searchCoverage": "Pinned OpenConnector Bitbucket connector is OAuth 2.0 only. Native recipe auth cannot express authorizeUrl/tokenUrl. Official API tokens and repository access tokens exist but are not the pinned authTypes and are not invented as an API-key mapping. Dated incident search on 2026-09-13 found Cloud availability incidents and a customer-hosted ESA report, not an unresolved Bitbucket Cloud compromise.",
    "incidents": [
      {
        "date": "2025-11-11",
        "source": "https://bitbucket.status.atlassian.com/incidents/xwqvgfv2wfqw",
        "finding": "Bitbucket Cloud availability incident caused by a feature-flag evaluation change. Website, APIs, and Git hosting were unavailable for about 90 minutes. Recorded as historical non-China operational coverage, not a customer-data compromise.",
        "limitation": "This is not a breach-free claim; live authentication remains unverified."
      }
    ],
    "remainingGates": [
      "credentials: OAuth-only without a native oauth block we can express (no authorizeUrl/tokenUrl in native auth setup; pinned authTypes are oauth2 only; official API tokens/app passwords are a different auth shape and are not invented here)",
      "live authentication unverified"
